From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] advapi32: LookupAccountSidW of the first user's SID does not ask GetUserNameW

GetUserNameW on an impersonating thread looks the token's user up with LookupAccountSidW (1709), which named the first user's SID (RID 1000) with GetUserNameW: the two recursed until the stack overflowed. Zoom's MSI custom action, impersonating while it connected to the Task Scheduler, died and the install failed (msiexec 67). The name is now the process's user (WINEUSERNAME), as GetUserNameW gave it unimpersonated.
---
diff --git a/dlls/advapi32/security.c b/dlls/advapi32/security.c
index 6b78d6a..f09e23f 100644
--- a/dlls/advapi32/security.c
+++ b/dlls/advapi32/security.c
@@ -1329,7 +1329,16 @@ LookupAccountSidW(
                         case 1000:	/* first user account */
                             size = UNLEN + 1;
                             account_name = malloc(size * sizeof(WCHAR));
+                            /* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 6104): the process's user, not GetUserNameW, which
+                             * for an impersonating thread looks its token's user up here -- the same SID:
+                             * the two called each other until the stack overflowed (Zoom's installer's
+                             * custom action, impersonating, connecting to the Task Scheduler) */
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_LOOKUP_RECURSES
                             if (GetUserNameW(account_name, &size))
+#else
+                            if (account_name && GetEnvironmentVariableW(L"WINEUSERNAME", account_name, size) &&
+                                wcslen(account_name) < size)
+#endif
                                 ac = account_name;
                             else
                                 dm = NULL;
